@startuml services
!theme plain
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam nodesep 12
skinparam ranksep 40
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam packageStyle rectangle

title Services, grouped by the protocol they speak to a client

header
<b>FOUR PLANES, GROUPED BY PROTOCOL.</b>  Control is Mumble-over-TCP through the gateway.
Realtime is UDP or WebRTC <b>straight to the service</b>.  Bulk and admin are plain HTTP.
The gateway routes on the <b>16-bit type in the frame header</b> and never parses a payload, so a new service is a TOML block, not a release.
Shard keys: <b>scaling.puml</b>.   Gateway internals: <b>gateway-internals.puml</b>.   Rationale: <b>ARCHITECTURE.md</b>.
endheader

actor "legacy Mumble\nclient" as legacy #EEEEEE
actor "Fancy client" as fancy #E3F2FD
actor "**operator**" as oper #F3E5F5

component "**gateway**\nTLS · framing · rate limit\n**single writer per client socket**\nroutes by type, config-driven" as gw #FFE9D6

database "**session store**\n«gateway infrastructure, not a service»\nsequence number + bounded replay ring,\n**outliving any gateway pod**\nno client, no message type, no tier" as sstore #FFE0B2

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "**control plane** — gRPC only; no client reaches these directly" as CTRL #FAFAFA {

  package "essential — down means nobody logs in" as ESS #FFEBEE {
    component "**session-lifecycle**\nVersion · Authenticate · Reject\nServerSync · CodecVersion\nCryptSetup · Ping · timeouts\n0,2,3,4,5,15,21 + **1000**" as slife #FFF9C4
    component "**session-view**\n«the domain edge»\nthe composed live view of\nevery connected session.\nThe whole domain reads here.\nOwns nothing, writes nothing.\n**no client-facing type**" as sview #FFF9C4
    component "**permissions**\nACL eval\n+ request coalescing\n12,13,20 + **1001**" as perms #FFFFFF
    component "**metadata**\nchannels · tree\nmembership\n6,7 + **1002**" as meta #FFFFFF
    component "**userdata**\nprofiles\naccount settings\n8,9,14,18,22 + **1003**" as users #FFFFFF
    component "**server-config**\nruntime-mutable,\nper virtual server\n24,25 + **1013**" as scfg #FFFFFF
  }

  package "core — a feature dies" as CORE #FFF8E1 {
    component "**text**\nhistory: **UUIDv7**\n11 + **1005**" as text #FFFFFF
    component "**pchat**\nE2EE · key mgmt\nhistory: **UUIDv7**\n**1006**" as pchat #FFFFFF
    component "**moderation**\nbans · kicks\n10 + **1007**" as mod #FFFFFF
  }

  package "optional — nobody notices" as OPT #E8F5E9 {
    component "**plugins**  26 + **1010**\n**push** «FCM»  **1011**\n**audit** «UUIDv7»  **1012**\n**onboarding**  **1014**\n**social**  **1015**\n· reactions · receipts · typing\n· polls · watch · whiteboard\n**link-preview**  **1016**\n**context-actions**  16,17 + **1017**" as opt #FFFFFF
  }
}

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "**realtime plane** — UDP / WebRTC, client connects **directly**" as RT #FFEBEE {
  component "**voice**  «core»\nSFU · routing · **mints the ciphers**\nUDP 64738, its own socket\n1 (tunnel), 19 + **1004**\n—\nOpus **forwarded, never transcoded**\npayloads refcounted, never copied" as voice #FFFFFF
  component "**screenshare**  «optional»\nstr0m SFU · own ICE ports\n**1008**" as share #FFFFFF
}

' ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
package "**HTTP plane** — plain HTTPS, client connects **directly**" as HTTP #E8F5E9 {
  component "**files / http**  «optional»\nsigned URLs · uploads · blobs\nplugin binaries · audit exports\n**1009**" as files #FFFFFF
  component "**operator-api**  «admin»\nREST + OpenAPI\nauth **pluggable**: OIDC · JWT\nmTLS · token\ndefault **off**, localhost-bound" as opapi #F3E5F5
}

' ══════════════════════ control: TCP through the gateway ═══════════════════
legacy -[#000000]-> gw : **TCP 64738**\nTLS + framing
fancy  -[#000000]-> gw : **TCP 64738**\n+ **zstd** stream

gw -[#1565C0]-> CTRL  : gRPC
gw -[#1565C0]-> RT : gRPC — signalling\nand UDPTunnel only
gw -[#1565C0]-> files : gRPC — mint a signed URL
note on link #E3F2FD
  Payload forwarded **verbatim** — already protobuf, never
  re-encoded. Unix socket when co-located, TCP when not.
  **Circuit breaker per service**, inbound shed by `tier`.
  **RESUME**: a sequence number per session in a store that
  outlives the pod, so a rolling deploy is not 10 000
  simultaneous full floods.
end note

gw -[#F57C00]-> sstore : stamp · replay
note on link #FFE0B2
  **Why this is not in a tier.** `tier` decides what the gateway does
  when a dependency is down, and both answers are wrong here:
  **essential** would reject logins over a lost *optimisation*, and
  **optional** claims nobody notices — false, because its absence
  bites at the worst possible moment and the resulting herd can
  saturate metadata, which *is* essential.
  It is not a service at all: no client reaches it, it has no
  message type, and it is never scaled on its own. It is the
  gateway's own durable state, externalised so a pod can die.
  **Legacy clients can never RESUME**, so staggered drain and
  jittered reconnect hints are required regardless. This store
  optimises a path that must already survive without it — which is
  what "not essential" means.
  It is reported in readiness as a **warning**, never as unready.
end note

' ══════════════════════ realtime: no gateway hop ═══════════════════════════
legacy -[#C62828]-> voice : **UDP 64738**
fancy  -[#C62828]-> voice : **UDP 64738**
note on link #FFEBEE
  Same port, different protocol, **different process** — murmur
  binds these separately, Server.cpp:125 vs 193. So audio never
  traverses the gateway. Only UDPTunnel, the UDP-blocked
  fallback, comes through the control plane.
  **Affinity is by channel, never by client.**
  Per-packet cost is **N seals, not one**: every listener needs
  the frame under their own key.
end note

fancy -[#C62828]-> share : **WebRTC / ICE**
note on link #FFEBEE
  Media direct to the SFU; only signalling via the gateway.
  str0m is **ICE-lite**: it ignores trickled candidates, its own
  rides in the SDP answer. Never trickle ICE through the control
  plane, and retry offers until answered.
end note

' ══════════════════════ HTTP: bulk and admin ═══════════════════════════════
fancy  -[#2E7D32]-> files : **HTTPS**, signed URL
legacy -[#2E7D32]-> files : **HTTPS**
oper   -[#6A1B9A]-> opapi : **HTTPS + REST**

' ══════════════════════ the two halves of session ══════════════════════════
slife -[#1565C0].-> sview : session up · down · moved · flags
slife -[#1565C0]-> voice : mint a CryptSetup payload
note on link #FFEBEE
  **Voice mints the key, because voice is what uses it** to seal
  UDP. Key material never crosses a service boundary; a
  client-requested resync takes the same path.
end note

' ══════════════════════ session-view is the edge for the domain ════════════
CORE -[#1565C0].-> sview : **one** composed snapshot stream
OPT  -[#1565C0].-> sview
RT   -[#1565C0].-> sview
gw   -[#1565C0].-> sview
note on link #FFF9C4
  **Read here and nowhere else** — otherwise every service depends
  on four others, with four caches each to keep warm.
  It **forwards but never decides**, and is a
  **subscription hub, not a proxy** — nothing on the audio path
  makes a request.
  **Every mailbox is bounded**, with a shed policy.
end note

sview -[#1565C0].-> users : profile changes
sview -[#1565C0].-> perms : groups + current-channel perms
sview -[#1565C0].-> meta  : channel · tree · membership
sview -[#1565C0].-> scfg  : limits · bandwidth

note bottom of sview #FFF9C4
  **A stale deny is safe; a stale grant is a security bug.**
  A revocation invalidates the view before it is acknowledged;
  a grant may arrive lazily.
end note

opapi -[#6A1B9A]-> ESS : gRPC, **operator** context
note on link #F3E5F5
  **The one thing that does not read through session-view**, and
  must not: that view is of *connected* users, while an operator
  edits registered accounts, offline bans and config.
  No service accepts an unauthenticated call.
  **Fail closed on audit.**
end note

note bottom of ESS #FFFFFF
  **Each service owns its own schema.** No service reads
  another's tables. One migration tool, many schemas.
end note

legend bottom
|= line |= plane |= transport |
| <color:#000000>**black**</color> | control | Mumble over TCP+TLS, through the gateway, ordered per client |
| <color:#C62828>**red**</color> | realtime | UDP or WebRTC, **direct to the service** |
| <color:#2E7D32>**green**</color> | bulk | HTTPS, signed URL, out of band |
| <color:#6A1B9A>**purple**</color> | admin | HTTPS + REST in, gRPC out, pluggable auth, default off |
| <color:#1565C0>**blue**</color> | internal | gRPC — solid is a call, dotted is a cached subscription |
endlegend

@enduml
